# The GRIND arm: one cycle, no AIs, driven straight into the rim and held there.
# SAMPLER, REPORT, CONFIGLINES, TAGHERE, CPURATE are substituted by run-arm.sh (comment
# lines are left alone). Not runnable on its own. Run it through run-arm.sh with this
# file as the 5th argument and, as the 4th, the four lines SP_SIZE_FACTOR -3,
# SP_NUM_AIS 0, CYCLE_RUBBER_TIME 0.1 and TIMESTEP_MAX 10 separated the way
# run-arm.sh's header says (a backslash-n pair per line break; the tripwire that
# refuses a doubled backslash reads comment lines too, which is why this comment
# does not spell it). Read docs/evidence/m6-lag/task3-mechanisms/README.md before
# changing a number here.
#
# WHAT IT MEASURES. Mechanism 2 of the M6 plan is the rubber path of
# gCycleMovement::TimestepCore -- the gSensor scan (GetMaxSpaceAhead) every step and
# the recursive re-simulation when a wall is near -- which scales with walls NEAR the
# cycle, not with the total trail. So: the smallest arena, no other cycle (the draw
# count is flat by construction), the idle human drives straight from its spawn into
# the rim and stays pressed against it. Per-second ms_to_first_draw before contact
# against after contact, with draws/frame flat, is the reading.
#
# WHY THESE CONFIG LINES, and why not the plan's. The match is welcome()'s tutorial
# match (gArmagetron.cpp; web/tools/perf/README.md, "What an arm is"), which assigns
# sg_rubberCycle = 5 for its duration AFTER autoexec.cfg is read, so the plan's
# CYCLE_RUBBER 50 cannot reach the game and is left out. What keeps the cycle alive
# at the rim is CYCLE_RUBBER_TIME: TimestepCore lets rubber decay by
# rubber /= (1 + ts/CYCLE_RUBBER_TIME) every step, so pressed against a wall at speed
# v the reservoir settles at v * CYCLE_RUBBER_TIME (15 * 0.1 = 1.5 of the 5 granted)
# and the cycle dies only when one step alone adds the missing 3.5 -- a frame over
# about 233 ms. (The plan's CYCLE_RUBBER_TIME 0 takes the else branch, rubber = 0
# every step: alive too, but the HUD's Rubber Used gauge reads 0 and cannot prove the
# grind; 0.1 shows a steady 30 % fill while grinding and 0 while free.)
# TIMESTEP_MAX 10 is for the kill switch below. SP_NUM_AIS 0 is honoured because
# welcome() sets autoNum 0. SP_SIZE_FACTOR -3 is the shipped value, written out so
# the arm says what it ran; welcome() lowers it by 2 more (a 0.177x arena, the rim
# 450 * 0.177 = 80 map units ahead of the spawn: 5.3 s at 15.0 after the 4 s
# countdown, so contact about 9.5 s after NEW_ROUND).
#
# THE KILL SWITCH. A lone cycle ends no round: with one team there is no winner
# (gGame.cpp Analysis: winner needs eTeam::teams.Len() > 1) and the round only
# advances when alive == 0, so a cycle that cannot die at the rim would hold round 1
# open for ever and round 2 would never start. The harness therefore kills it: a 1 s
# busy loop on the main thread (an eval: step; CDP has no timeout on it) makes the
# game's next timestep 1 s long, TIMESTEP_MAX 10 stops gGame::Timestep chopping it
# into 0.2 s pieces (sg_timestepMax), and one 1 s step against a wall needs 15 units
# of rubber where 5 are granted: death. A FREE cycle just moves 15 units and lives --
# so the death that follows each stall is itself proof the cycle was pressed against
# a wall. The stall is bracketed like a screenshot (sampler.js S.shot), so report.js
# drops its frame from every statistic; the span ends at the DEATH_ mark anyway.
# No ROUND_WINNER is written for a winnerless round; report.js closes a round at the
# next NEW_ROUND (closed_by: next_round), which is what the until: steps wait for.
#
# ROUND 1 is setup and is NOT measured: the tutorial's two key presses after the
# countdown (arm.steps.tmpl says why the 3 s), the throttle, the first kill.
wait:800
eval:SAMPLER
eval:(()=>{const p='/data/webdefaults/autoexec.cfg';const cur=Module.FS.readFile(p,{encoding:'utf8'});const add='\n# perf arm TAGHERE\nMAX_FPS 1000\nCONFIGLINES\n';Module.FS.writeFile(p,cur+add);return 'autoexec.cfg patched: '+JSON.stringify(add)})()
eval:window.AA_START()
until:1:90000:[BOOT] autostart
wait:9000
tap:#tapzone
wait:3000
tap:#tapzone
wait:3500
tap:#tapzone
wait:2000
until:1:120000:[L] NEW_ROUND
mark:ROUND-1-SETUP-NOT-MEASURED
wait:3000
key:Right:1
key:Left:1
wait:1500
eval:__fps.shot('r1-after-tutorial-keys','begin')
shot:r1-after-tutorial-keys
eval:__fps.shot('r1-after-tutorial-keys','end')
cpu:CPURATE
mark:THROTTLE-ON
wait:7000
eval:__fps.shot('kill-stall-r1','begin')
eval:(()=>{const t0=performance.now();while(performance.now()-t0<1000){}return 'kill stall '+Math.round(performance.now()-t0)+' ms on the main thread'})()
eval:__fps.shot('kill-stall-r1','end')
until:2:60000:[L] NEW_ROUND
mark:ROUND-2-GRIND
wait:2000
eval:__fps.shot('g-02s-before-rim','begin')
shot:g-02s-before-rim
eval:__fps.shot('g-02s-before-rim','end')
wait:4000
eval:__fps.shot('g-06s-approach','begin')
shot:g-06s-approach
eval:__fps.shot('g-06s-approach','end')
wait:6000
eval:__fps.shot('g-12s-grinding','begin')
shot:g-12s-grinding
eval:__fps.shot('g-12s-grinding','end')
wait:8000
eval:__fps.shot('g-20s-grinding','begin')
shot:g-20s-grinding
eval:__fps.shot('g-20s-grinding','end')
wait:10000
eval:__fps.shot('g-30s-grinding','begin')
shot:g-30s-grinding
eval:__fps.shot('g-30s-grinding','end')
wait:8000
eval:__fps.shot('kill-stall-r2','begin')
eval:(()=>{const t0=performance.now();while(performance.now()-t0<1000){}return 'kill stall '+Math.round(performance.now()-t0)+' ms on the main thread'})()
eval:__fps.shot('kill-stall-r2','end')
until:3:60000:[L] NEW_ROUND
mark:GRIND-OVER
wait:1000
eval:REPORT
